            <ArticleTitle>Evidence-based practice guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of lumbar spinal conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-37</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Low back pain remains one of the most common patient complaints. It can exist alone or with the presence of lower extremity symptoms. Review of evidence-based guidelines will assist primary care providers in the identification and treatment of various lumbar disorders in addition to ruling out specific lumbar spinal pathologies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
